  "title": "Founding of the Royal Society",
  "summary": "The Royal Society's first meeting took place on 28 November 1660, after a lecture at Gresham College in London by its Professor of Astronomy, Christopher Wren. The Fellowship was to concern itself with natural philosophy. It received a royal charter in 1662, and a further charter in 1663 gave its full name.",
